+**Published ASERT test-vector subset**
+
+These numeric expected outcomes come from the [BCHN ASERT test-vector directory](https://download.bitcoincashnode.org/misc/data/asert/test_vectors/), linked by the [aserti3-2d specification](https://upgradespecs.bitcoincashnode.org/2020-11-15-asert/). Each run's anchor target is retained, timestamps are reduced by its anchor-parent timestamp, and heights by its anchor height. Expected bits are copied directly, not regenerated by the implementation.
+
+The subset retains the first/last ten rows and 32 evenly distributed positions from each run, removing overlaps. This covers steady schedules, stochastic/variable hashrate, limit saturation, and large absolute height/time conventions. C++ tests and the Python reference both check the subset. Absolute upstream heights beyond eCash's signed 32-bit index are reduced to their representable height difference for the pure arithmetic test.
+
+The entire twelve-run collection was also verified independently. To reproduce after downloading the runs, use `python3 contrib/daa_reference.py --upstream-dir /path/to/runs`. Regenerate both C++ headers with `--write-vectors`. No network fetch is needed for the checked-in subset.
+
+SHA256 and original row counts:
+
